body: |-
  ## Sprint structure
  - Sprint 1 (~10 days): soft-block primitive + authority MCP tools — Builder + Architect + Jinx + Loid + Documentor + Rune
  - Sprint 2 (~12 days): tier-split + sovereign notebooks + cross-refs (one PR set, notebook MCP surface lockstep) — Loid leads + Builder + Architect + Documentor + Jinx
  - Sprint 3 (~10 days): hook-orchestrator + 4 new Rune MCP tools + compliance-check→aspect-report rename + session-start ambient pass + Failure Ledger — Builder + Rune + Loid + Documentor + Jinx
  - Plus 2 soak weeks between sprints for telemetry collection and parity validation

  ## Critical path
  Soft-block trunk → all authority work depends on it. Tier-split + cross-refs parallel-safe but MUST merge before Sprint 2 closes (notebook MCP surface gains both `tier:` and `refs:` parameters in lockstep).

  ## 5 user-judgment open calls
  - #3 promotion threshold (recommended: ≥2 distinct originProject + content-generality + applied ≥3 + confidence ≥0.75)
  - #4 pre-seed Rune's 6 patterns at confidence 0.5-0.7 with loid-seed provenance
  - #7 revoke gate user-only
  - #11 aspect-report-history rename: parallel writes vs hard rename + alias-reader
  - **#14 PARA 451 Phase B vs PARA 551** — must resolve before Sprint 1 ends (Phase B design kickoff)

  ## What's NOT in v6.1 (v6.2+)
  8 items confirmed deferred: paradigm_optout_register, paradigm_severity_emit, JSONLogic unblock predicates, override-cluster auto-coaching, per-component metric snapshot to lore, auto-promote tier-1, Auto-author/Guard beyond Advise, drift remediation of this repo's 316 anchors.
